      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZOEHRER (10) debuted in a strong maiden at Sandown Lakeside, in the market and boxing on well along the inside for a narrow fourth. There's already been strong form out of that with Somethings Burnin' a moral beaten next time and Zambales winning over the weekend. Up in trip should suit and he gets every hope. SHINY DIAMOND (4) wasn't beaten far first up at Sale over 1100m in a bunched finish. Much better suited this trip and will take catching. HEDJET (1) resumes for his Aus debut. The form out of his two runs in Ireland are outstanding - both winners have gone on to G1 success. Very wary of any support for the McDonald yard. ZVEREV (2) is a Tarzino gelding for the Eurell yard who has won a trial and can figure. ENCHILADA (7) next best on debut.",
